# AWS Services — Detailed Interview Notes

---

## 1. EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)

**What it is:** Resizable virtual machines (VMs) in the cloud used to host applications, servers, and workloads.

**Key Concepts:**
- **AMI (Amazon Machine Image)** – template containing OS + software config used to launch instances. Can create custom AMI (golden image) for faster, consistent deployments.
- **Instance Types** – categorized by use case:
  - General Purpose (t2, t3, m5) – balanced CPU/Memory
  - Compute Optimized (c5) – high CPU workloads
  - Memory Optimized (r5, x1) – databases, caching
  - Storage Optimized (i3, d2) – high I/O workloads
  - GPU Instances (p3, g4) – ML/graphics workloads
- **Purchasing Options:**
  - On-Demand – pay per hour/second, no commitment
  - Reserved Instances – 1 or 3 year commitment, up to 72% discount
  - Spot Instances – bid on unused capacity, up to 90% discount, can be terminated anytime
  - Savings Plans – flexible pricing model committing to consistent usage
  - Dedicated Hosts/Instances – physical server dedicated to you (compliance needs)
- **EBS (Elastic Block Store)** – persistent block storage attached to EC2 (like a virtual hard disk). Types: gp3 (general SSD), io2 (high IOPS), st1 (throughput HDD), sc1 (cold HDD). Supports snapshots (backup to S3).
- **Instance Store** – temporary storage physically attached to host, data lost on stop/terminate.
- **Security Groups** – virtual firewall at instance level; stateful (return traffic auto-allowed); only ALLOW rules.
- **Elastic IP** – static public IP that can be remapped between instances.
- **Placement Groups:**
  - Cluster – low latency, same AZ
  - Spread – across distinct hardware, max 7 instances/AZ
  - Partition – large distributed workloads (Hadoop, Cassandra)
- **User Data** – bootstrap script run at first launch (install packages, configs).
- **Auto Scaling Group (ASG)** – automatically adds/removes EC2 instances based on demand (CPU, custom CloudWatch metric, schedule). Uses Launch Template/Configuration.
- **Load Balancer Integration** – ALB (HTTP/HTTPS, Layer 7, path/host based routing), NLB (Layer 4, ultra-low latency, static IP), CLB (legacy).
- **EC2 Instance Metadata (IMDS)** – 169.254.169.254 endpoint, gives instance info (IAM role creds, AMI ID, etc). IMDSv2 (token-based) recommended for security.

**Common Interview Qs:**
- Difference between Security Group and NACL?
- On-Demand vs Reserved vs Spot?
- How does Auto Scaling work with Load Balancer & CloudWatch?
- EBS vs Instance Store?

