## 3. S3 (Simple Storage Service)

**What it is:** Object storage service to store & retrieve any amount of data from anywhere; highly durable & scalable.

**Key Concepts:**
- **Bucket** – container for objects; name must be globally unique.
- **Object** – file + metadata; max size 5TB per object.
- **Storage Classes:**
  - Standard – frequent access
  - Intelligent-Tiering – auto moves data between tiers based on access pattern
  - Standard-IA (Infrequent Access) – cheaper, retrieval fee
  - One Zone-IA – cheaper, single AZ only (less durable)
  - Glacier Instant/Flexible/Deep Archive – archival, cheapest, retrieval time varies (minutes to hours)
- **Versioning** – keeps multiple versions of an object; protects against accidental deletion/overwrite.
- **Lifecycle Policies** – automatically transition/delete objects after X days (e.g., move to Glacier after 30 days).
- **Replication:**
  - CRR (Cross-Region Replication) – replicate to bucket in different region
  - SRR (Same-Region Replication) – replicate within same region
- **Encryption:**
  - SSE-S3 – AWS-managed keys
  - SSE-KMS – AWS KMS managed keys (audit trail)
  - SSE-C – customer-provided keys
  - Client-side encryption – encrypt before upload
- **Access Control:**
  - Bucket Policy – JSON resource-based policy at bucket level
  - IAM Policy – user/role-based
  - ACL – legacy, object/bucket level permissions
  - Block Public Access – account/bucket setting to prevent accidental public exposure
- **Static Website Hosting** – host static HTML/CSS/JS websites directly from S3.
- **Event Notifications** – trigger Lambda, SQS, SNS on object create/delete events.
- **Multipart Upload** – upload large files in parts parallelly (recommended >100MB).
- **Presigned URLs** – temporary URL granting time-limited access to private object.
- **S3 Transfer Acceleration** – faster uploads using CloudFront edge locations.
- Durability: 99.999999999% (11 9's); Availability: 99.99%.

**Common Interview Qs:**
- Difference between Bucket Policy and IAM Policy?
- How does S3 versioning protect data?
- Storage class selection based on access pattern?
- How would you secure an S3 bucket?

