## 15. Other Important AWS Services (frequently asked in interviews)

- **CloudFormation** – Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using JSON/YAML templates; native AWS alternative to Terraform; supports Stacks, Change Sets, Nested Stacks, StackSets (multi-account/region deployment).
- **CloudFront** – Content Delivery Network (CDN); caches content at edge locations globally to reduce latency; integrates with S3 (OAC/OAI for private access), ALB, custom origins; supports signed URLs/cookies for restricted content.
- **SNS (Simple Notification Service)** – Pub/Sub messaging service; publishes messages to multiple subscribers (email, SMS, Lambda, SQS, HTTP endpoint) simultaneously — fan-out pattern.
- **SQS (Simple Queue Service)** – Message queue used to decouple microservices/apps; Standard Queue (at-least-once, best-effort ordering) vs FIFO Queue (exactly-once, strict ordering); Dead Letter Queue for failed messages; Visibility Timeout concept important.
- **KMS (Key Management Service)** – centrally manage & control encryption keys (CMK - Customer Master Keys); integrates with S3, EBS, RDS, Lambda for encryption at rest.
- **Secrets Manager** – securely store, retrieve, and automatically rotate secrets (DB credentials, API keys) — more advanced than Parameter Store (auto-rotation built-in).
- **Systems Manager (SSM)** – Parameter Store (config/secrets storage), Session Manager (SSH-less secure shell access to EC2), Patch Manager (automated patching), Run Command.
- **Elastic Load Balancer (ELB):**
  - ALB – Layer 7, HTTP/HTTPS, path-based & host-based routing, supports WebSockets
  - NLB – Layer 4, TCP/UDP, ultra-low latency, static IP support
  - CLB – Legacy, being phased out
- **Auto Scaling Group (ASG)** – automatically launches/terminates EC2 based on demand; uses scaling policies (target tracking, step scaling, scheduled scaling).
- **DynamoDB** – fully managed, serverless NoSQL database; single-digit millisecond latency; supports on-demand & provisioned capacity, Global Tables (multi-region), DAX (in-memory caching layer), Streams (change data capture).
- **EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service)** – managed Kubernetes control plane; supports EC2 and Fargate worker nodes; use when you need full Kubernetes ecosystem/portability across clouds.
- **CodeDeploy** – automates application deployment to EC2, on-prem, Lambda, ECS; supports Blue/Green and In-place deployment strategies; uses appspec.yml.
- **CodeCommit** – AWS's own fully managed private Git repository service (note: AWS has been deprecating new customer onboarding for this — worth mentioning if asked).
- **AWS Organizations** – centrally manage multiple AWS accounts; apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) to restrict permissions account-wide; consolidated billing.
- **Cost Explorer / AWS Budgets** – visualize spending trends, forecast costs, set budget alerts.
- **WAF (Web Application Firewall)** – protects web apps from common exploits like SQL Injection, XSS; works with CloudFront/ALB/API Gateway; rule-based (managed rule groups or custom).
- **AWS Shield** – DDoS protection; Standard (free, automatic) and Advanced (paid, 24/7 DDoS response team, cost protection).
- **AWS Config** – tracks configuration changes of resources over time; evaluates compliance against defined rules (e.g., "S3 buckets must not be public").
- **EFS (Elastic File System)** – managed NFS-based shared file storage; can be mounted across multiple EC2 instances/AZs simultaneously (unlike EBS which is single-instance).
- **API Gateway** – fully managed service to create, publish, and secure REST/HTTP/WebSocket APIs; integrates tightly with Lambda for serverless APIs; supports throttling, caching, custom authorizers.
- **Elastic Beanstalk** – PaaS to quickly deploy & manage applications without worrying about underlying infra (auto-handles EC2, ELB, ASG, RDS provisioning).
- **Step Functions** – orchestrate multiple Lambda functions/AWS services into visual workflows (state machines) for complex business logic.
- **X-Ray** – distributed tracing service to analyze/debug microservices/applications (see request flow across services).

